    {
      "bench_id": "query.covering.advantage_growth",
      "status": "skipped",
      "reason": "Skipped: Bench cannot demonstrate its claim on this generator's data shape. generate_scale_data emits exactly 2 quads per entity (vitaltype + hasName) in a single context, so the probe predicate matches ~50% of the table. At that selectivity PG18 picks a Bitmap Heap Scan via a predicate-leading index and never uses idx_*_quad_ctx_pred at all \u2014 measured WITH vs WITHOUT the covering index are byte-identical (2938/2938, 8811/8811, 26426/26426 buffers at 100K/300K/900K entities, ratio 1.0x). This is a property of the synthetic data, NOT a covering-index regression: the index-only gate on the realistic lead dataset (test_covering_indexes.py, moved there by 701c08b) is unaffected. Re-enable once the generator grows a predicate-cardinality knob so a selective probe exists \u2014 see performance_regression_tracking_plan.md."
